 is also not an image  so if I exit  full screen mode here and resize the  window this will resize accordingly  intent and line wrap right we have  support for graphics both  two-dimensional and three-dimensional so  if you have something like this you can  take this and rotate it interactively  and of course we support various  interactive user interface elements of  of notebooks so in simple case it could  be like a button here that when you  press it prints a large number but you  can build more more complex user  interfaces either using low level  constructs like button and dynamic  module and so on order is a very nice  high level sort of function that that  constructs user interfaces for you just  manipulate so if you do something like  this you get back a manipulate that is  interactive right in my browser now can  drag the sliders I can move around  locators and it just works so that's the  general idea of cloud notebooks and I  wanna highlight some things that have  happened over the past year or so and  very big focus of ours has certainly  been stability to make the whole system  more robust so a few things you  shouldn't see anymore now is this  warning it says that your session timed  out and then you had to refresh the  whole page there was a bit annoying  there was also problem where if you kept  the manipulated open for a long time  sometimes you got initialization timed  out and they all had to do basically  with the client and the server getting  out of sync after a while and then there  was no good way for them to communicate  anymore  not they were actually separate issues  and and really not trivial to solve but  I think we did now and and so these  problems should be should be gone now  and of course we're making various  improvements to make all of notebook  rendering more robust but we realized  that there's probably always gonna be  some limit of what you can do in a web  browser because after all it's a very  hostile environment to do this 